WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.621
Hi! Who are you?

2
00:00:09.622 --> 00:00:13.232
I'm a beaver.

3
00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:17.394
Beavers are big rodents.

4
00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:23.417
Rodents have sharp front teeth.

5
00:00:23.418 --> 00:00:27.265
Where do you live?

6
00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:31.849
Beavers live in North America and Europe.

7
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.451
We like to be in fresh water.

8
00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:42.176
Can beavers really cut down trees?

9
00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:47.231
Yes. We use our sharp teeth for that.

10
00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:51.583
We chew through tree trunks.

11
00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:57.493
And then . . . Crash!

12
00:00:57.494 --> 00:01:02.520
What do you do with the trees?

13
00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:05.799
We eat tree bark.

14
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.818
We also use the branches to build things.

15
00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:13.828
What do you build?

16
00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:18.048
We build dams.

17
00:01:18.049 --> 00:01:23.185
Our dams stop streams and make ponds.

18
00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:27.743
We build our homes in those ponds.

19
00:01:27.744 --> 00:01:32.210
What are your homes made of?

20
00:01:32.211 --> 00:01:36.362
They are made of sticks and mud.

21
00:01:36.363 --> 00:01:40.861
Beavers can also dig canals.

22
00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:45.190
We use the canals to carry our branches.

23
00:01:45.191 --> 00:01:50.550
Your tail looks strong.

24
00:01:50.551 --> 00:01:56.532
Our tails help us swim.

25
00:01:56.533 --> 00:02:02.676
We also slap the water with them.

26
00:02:02.677 --> 00:02:11.007
That warns other beavers that enemies are near.

27
00:02:11.008 --> 00:02:13.081
Uh-oh!

28
00:02:13.082 --> 00:02:23.118
An enemy is coming now!

29
00:02:23.119 --> 00:02:29.558
Good-bye, Beaver!

